{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וזרח משעיר", :translit "v'zarach mi-se'ir", :gloss "and He shone from Seir"} {:he "וזרח בחשך", :translit "v'zarach ba-choshech", :gloss "and He shone in darkness"} {:he "וזרח השמש", :translit "v'zarach ha-shemesh", :gloss "and the sun shone"} {:he "מצות ה' ברה מאירת עינים", :translit "mitzvat Hashem barah me'irat eynayim", :gloss "the commandment of YHWH is clear, enlightening the eyes"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["וזרח משעיר" "וזרח בחשך" "וזרח השמש"]}], :frame {:text "The tradition that God offered the Torah to the nations before Israel appears in Avodah Zarah 2b. The specific motif that He first offered it to Esau (Seir) and they refused is developed in Sifrei Devarim 343. The verse cited as proof, 'the commandment of YHWH is clear, enlightening the eyes' (Psalms 19:9), links the acceptance of Torah to light versus the darkness suffered by those who refused it.", :sources ["Avodah Zarah 2b" "Sifrei Devarim 343" "Psalms 19:9"]}} {:quotes [{:he "הופיע", :translit "hofia", :gloss "He appeared"} {:he "הופיא מהר פארן", :translit "hofia me-har Paran", :gloss "He appeared from Mount Paran"} {:he "מציון מכלל יופי אלהים הופיע", :translit "mi-Tziyon michlal yofi Elokim hofia", :gloss "out of Zion, the perfection of beauty, God appeared"} {:he "אל נקמות ה' אל נקמות הופיע", :translit "El nekamot Hashem El nekamot hofia", :gloss "God of vengeance, YHWH; God of vengeance, appeared"} {:he "מציון מכלל יופי אלהים הופיע", :translit "mi-Tziyon michlal yofi Elokim hofia", :gloss "out of Zion, the perfection of beauty, God appeared"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["הופיא מהר פארן" "מציון מכלל יופי אלהים הופיע" "אל נקמות ה' אל נקמות הופיע"]}], :frame {:text "The root הופיע (He appeared) links three verses across the Bible: its use at Sinai/Paran (Deuteronomy 33:2), the verse 'Out of Zion, the perfection of beauty, God shone forth' (Psalms 50:2), and 'O God of vengeance, YHWH... shine forth' (Psalms 94:1). Ba'al HaTurim reads these as a progression: the nations who refused the Torah receive punishment, while Israel merits the radiance of Torah from Zion.", :sources ["Psalms 50:2" "Psalms 94:1" "Deuteronomy 33:2"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מרבבות", :translit "m'rivavot", :gloss "of myriads"} {:he "ואתה מרבבות קדש", :translit "v'atah m'rivavot kodesh", :gloss "and You are myriads of holiness"} {:he "לא אירא מרבבות עם", :translit "lo ira m'rivavot am", :gloss "I will not fear myriads of people"} {:he "כי אתה ה' מרבבות קדש", :translit "ki atah Hashem m'rivavot kodesh", :gloss "for You, YHWH, are myriads of holiness"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ואתה מרבבות קדש" "לא אירא מרבבות עם"]} {:kind :other, :note "Cites a third occurrence כי אתה ה' מרבבות קדש as the reason the first provides help."}], :frame {:text "The recurrence of מרבבות ('myriads') across Deuteronomy 33:2, Psalms 3:7, and the phrase כי אתה ה' מרבבות קדש creates an intertextual link. Ba'al HaTurim reads the shared root as proof that God's myriad holy ones, announced at Sinai in Deuteronomy 33:2, are the very force the psalmist trusts to come to his aid.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 33:2" "Psalms 3:7"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["וזרח משעיר" "וזרח בחשך" "וזרח השמש"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "וזרח משעיר", :refs ["Deuteronomy 33:2"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "וזרח בחשך", :refs ["Isaiah 58:10"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "וזרח השמש", :refs ["Ecclesiastes 1:5"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["הופיא מהר פארן" "מציון מכלל יופי אלהים הופיע" "אל נקמות ה' אל נקמות הופיע"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "הופיא מהר פארן", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "מציון מכלל יופי אלהים הופיע", :refs ["Psalms 50:2"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "אל נקמות ה' אל נקמות הופיע", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ואתה מרבבות קדש" "לא אירא מרבבות עם"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ואתה מרבבות קדש", :refs ["Deuteronomy 33:2"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "לא אירא מרבבות עם", :refs ["Psalms 3:7"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Cites a third occurrence כי אתה ה' מרבבות קדש as the reason the first provides help.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:41:24.715488640Z", :model "glm-5.2"}